<body>
    <h1>How to Deploy IGEL OS 12 with PXE</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-m=
acro-note">
<style>[data-colorid=3Dbcz7nicgoi]{color:#161616} html[data-color-mode=3Dda=
rk] [data-colorid=3Dbcz7nicgoi]{color:#e9e9e9}[data-colorid=3Dehn9dhbpku]{c=
olor:#161616} html[data-color-mode=3Ddark] [data-colorid=3Dehn9dhbpku]{colo=
r:#e9e9e9}</style><span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warni=
ng confluence-information-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<h3 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withPXE-InternetAccessRequired">Internet Acces=
s Required</h3>
<p>In contrast to a typical PXE environment, the installation of IGEL OS 12=
 requires Internet access because the endpoint devices must be able to reac=
h the IGEL App Portal.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withPXE-Prerequisites">Prerequisites</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Your devices meet the requirements for IGEL OS 12. For further informati=
on, see <em>Hardware &gt; Supported Devices &gt; IGEL OS 12 Hardware Suppor=
t &gt; Devices Supported by IGEL OS 12</em></p></li>
<li>
<p>Your devices are able to boot via the network</p></li>
<li>
<p>Your devices are in a network with Internet access</p></li>
<li>
<p>A DHCP Server is available in your network</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withPXE-RetrievingtheRequiredFilesfromtheOSCZI=
PFile">Retrieving the Required Files from the OSC ZIP File</h2>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Open a web browser, go to <a class=3D"external-link" href=3D"https://www=
.igel.com/software-downloads/cosmos/" rel=3D"nofollow">https://www.igel.com=
/software-downloads/cosmos/</a>, and select the folder <strong>OS 12 BASE S=
YSTEM IMAGE FOR PXE</strong>.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Download the ZIP file (e.g. <code>osc_12.2.1_pxe.zip</code>) and extract=
 it. <br>
We will distribute the required files to their appropriate locations later =
on.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withPXE-SettinguptheDHCPServer"><span class=3D=
"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"6ef6c825-eb9b-4481-aa62-76fd85965944">S=
etting up the DHCP Server</span></h2>
<p>When the devices are powered on, they need to be directed to the TFTP se=
rver that provides the low-level files required for booting. This is done b=
y the DHCP server. In our example, we use a Microsoft Windows DHCP server; =
other DHCP can be used as well.</p>
<p>In the following, we will create three vendor classes, two for UEFI and =
one for BIOS.&nbsp;</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>On your Windows server, go to <strong>DHCP</strong> and right-click on <=
strong>IPv4</strong>.<br></p></li>
<li>
<p>Define each vendor class as follows:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>In the <strong>DHCP Vendor Classes</strong> dialog, click <strong>Add</s=
trong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Enter the data according to the vendor class you are creating:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Vendor class for UEFI on an x86 architecture:<br></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Display name</strong>: <code>PXEClient (UEFI x86)</code></p></li=
>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: <code>PXEClient:Arch:00006</code></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Vendor class for UEFI on an x64 architecture:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Display name</strong>: <code>PXEClient (UEFI x64)</code></p></li=
>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: <code>PXEClient:Arch:00007</code></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Vendor class for BIOS on x86 and x64 architectures:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Display name</strong>: <code>PXEClient (BIOS x86 &amp; x64)</cod=
e></p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Description</strong>: <code>PXEClient:Arch:00000</code><br></p><=
span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper conflue=
nce-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluenc=
e-content-image-border image-center" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"=
16c6d64639758dcbc905c4678f8f6cb174d73beee43d3fa591b4dccba8ff585d" data-imag=
e-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302642=
/image-2023-9-27_15-59-47.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364687=
498&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"799" data-width=3D"12=
80" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73308991=
" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachmen=
t" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2023-9-27_15-59-47.png" data=
-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-con=
tent-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302642" data=
-linked-resource-container-version=3D"6" data-media-id=3D"c230b33b-d3a7-4b2=
a-9bfc-5fac0d6c5d17" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"292"></span>
<p></p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p>Perform the following steps for each vendor class you have created:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Right-click <strong>Scope ([IP address]) DHCP range &gt; Policies</stron=
g> and select <strong>New Policy</strong> from the context menu.</p></li>
<li>
<p>At <strong>Policy Name</strong>, enter the name exactly as you did for t=
he vendor classes, i.e, once <code>PXEClient (UEFI x86)</code>, once, <code=
>PXEClient (UEFI x64)</code>, and once <code>PXEClient (x86 &amp; x64)</cod=
e>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>In the <strong>Configure Conditions for the policy</strong> screen, clic=
k <strong>Add</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>In the <strong>Add/Edit Condition</strong> dialog, click the&nbsp;drop-d=
own menu <strong>Value:</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Select the appropriate vendor class.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Activate <strong>Append wildcard</strong>. click <strong>Add</strong> an=
d then <strong>OK</strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Click <strong>Next</strong>,</p></li>
<li>
<p>Answer the question <strong>Do you want to configure an IP address range=
 for the policy?</strong> with <strong>No</strong> and click <strong>Next</=
strong>.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Activate option <strong>060</strong> and edit it, according to the polic=
y you are at:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>For <code>PXEClient (UEFI x86)</code>, enter <code>PXEClient</code>.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>For <code>PXEClient (UEFI x64)</code>, enter <code>PXEClient</code>.</p>=
</li>
<li>
<p>For <code>PXEClient (BIOS x86 &amp; x64)</code>, leave the option empty.=
</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p>Activate option <strong>066</strong> and enter the Fully Qualified Domai=
n Name (FQDN) or the IP address of your <span data-colorid=3D"ehn9dhbpku">T=
FTP </span>server.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Activate option <strong>067</strong> and enter the path to the appropria=
te .efi file on your TFTP server. For example, this might be <code>grub/boo=
tx64.efi</code> for the <code>PXEClient (UEFI x64)</code> vendor class if y=
ou are using GRUB as the bootloader.<br>
&nbsp;</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p>Review your <strong>Scope Options</strong>; they should be similar to th=
is:</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper=
 confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image c=
onfluence-content-image-border image-center" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy"=
 src=3D"8cf3f6a6812bd7574357e382caf2c99ece4d8dfc41c5697feac483b73cf3d982" d=
ata-image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/=
73302642/image-2023-9-27_16-0-7.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716=
364687489&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"831" data-width=
=3D"1280" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73=
309080" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"att=
achment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2023-9-27_16-0-7.png" =
data-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource=
-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302642" =
data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"6" data-media-id=3D"2dd0a8df-81b8=
-4f23-92a6-998e4ed836f1" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"303"></span>
<p></p></li>
<li>
<p>Go to <strong>Server Options</strong>, add option <strong><span class=3D=
"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"42ef5625-4c45-40fc-9e8a-2c3a514d7651">0=
66</span></strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"42ef562=
5-4c45-40fc-9e8a-2c3a514d7651">,</span> and enter the&nbsp;Fully Qualified =
Domain Name (FQDN) or the IP address of your <span data-colorid=3D"bcz7nicg=
oi">TFTP</span>&nbsp;server.</p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wra=
pper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"co=
nfluence-embedded-image confluence-content-image-border image-center" width=
=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"645a2809c7341951ed984fa47719de72487372aa2c=
aa71a8feb6c13fc904f2a2" data-image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/w=
iki/download/attachments/73302642/image-2023-9-27_16-5-27.png?version=3D1&a=
mp;modificationDate=3D1716364687478&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data=
-height=3D"820" data-width=3D"1280" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" dat=
a-linked-resource-id=3D"73309152" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-l=
inked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"im=
age-2023-9-27_16-5-27.png" data-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net=
/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource=
-container-id=3D"73302642" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"6" dat=
a-media-id=3D"939bc202-8492-4905-b3fc-6d8886f42f7f" data-media-type=3D"file=
" height=3D"300"></span></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withPXE-DeployingtheTFTPServer">Deploying the =
TFTP Server</h2>
<p>In this step, we deploy that TFTP server that provides the bootloader an=
d a minimal OS that will load the higher-level components of IGEL OS.<br></=
p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Install a TFTP server, e.g. SolarWinds. see <a class=3D"external-link" h=
ref=3D"https://www.solarwinds.com/de/free-tools/free-tftp-server" rel=3D"no=
follow">https://www.solarwinds.com/de/free-tools/free-tftp-server</a><br></=
p></li>
<li>
<p>Specify the directory in which the PXE boot files will be stored, typica=
lly <code>C:\TFTP-Root</code><br></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-fil=
e-wrapper image-left-wrapper confluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D=
"confluence-embedded-image confluence-content-image-border image-left" widt=
h=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"514112469a52452fdf8366d85bd6a9b9f61fb6a75=
ca111bbfe83c53bb1111372" data-image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/=
wiki/download/attachments/73302642/image-2023-10-17_16-49-44.png?version=3D=
1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364687456&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" d=
ata-height=3D"827" data-width=3D"788" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" d=
ata-linked-resource-id=3D"73309150" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data=
-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"=
image-2023-10-17_16-49-44.png" data-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian=
.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-reso=
urce-container-id=3D"73302642" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"6"=
 data-media-id=3D"d63da82a-72fb-4e35-bc5c-cf00374263e7" data-media-type=3D"=
file" height=3D"491"></span>
<p></p></li>
<li>
<p>Copy the directories and files from the <code>tftp/</code> directory of =
your OSC ZIP file to the TFTP root directory, in our example <code>C:\TFTP-=
Root</code>. The directory structure must be preserved.<br>
The most important contents are:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>GRUB Bootloader for 64-bit EFI systems</p></li>
<li>
<p>GRUB Bootloader for i386/BIOS systems</p></li>
<li>
<p>Configuration file for GRUB Bootloader</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ol>
<h2 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withPXE-ProvidingthePXEConfigurationFile(pxe-c=
onfig.json)"><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"c8aa28f1-674=
8-4dec-8b37-124dfd166c82">Providing the PXE Configuration File (pxe-config.=
json)</span></h2>
<p>The file <code>pxe-config</code> is used at an early stage of the boot p=
rocess and will be provided by the TFTP server. It specifies the download p=
aths for specific necessary files, an authentication token for connecting w=
ith the IGEL App Portal, and the version of the Base System that is to be i=
nstalled.&nbsp;</p>
<p>First, we retrieve the file from the UMS, then we edit it to adapt it to=
 our environment. Afterward, we put it into the appropriate directory on th=
e TFTP server.</p>
<h3 id=3D"HowtoDeployIGELOS12withPXE-RetrievingtheFilefromtheUMS">Retrievin=
g the File from the UMS</h3>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p>Open the UMS Web App, go to <strong>Apps</strong> and click the <span cl=
ass=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-=
image confluence-content-image-inline" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"855b70b779bc=
f716040b9f878f9298e11f268a18a46192d9bb27e18579bb2123" data-image-src=3D"htt=
ps://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302642/image-2023-=
10-19_10-21-24.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364687450&amp;cac=
heVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"44" data-width=3D"42" data-unres=
olved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73308632" data-linked-=
resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked=
-resource-default-alias=3D"image-2023-10-19_10-21-24.png" data-base-url=3D"=
https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"=
image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"73302642" data-linked-resou=
rce-container-version=3D"6" data-media-id=3D"50e963b0-4d6f-44e1-a3c7-e584fd=
a05acf" data-media-type=3D"file" width=3D"42" height=3D"44"></span> icon.</=
p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper conflu=
ence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image confluen=
ce-content-image-border image-left" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"3=
